 ## `src/logger.ts` – shared logger
 
-It writes one JSON line per call to stdout (`level`, `message`, extra fields, ISO timestamp). The fields are restricted to `string | number | boolean`. No module currently uses it. Per this repo's logging policy, any logging added to users or orders must go through this logger, never `console.*`. It must identify people and orders only by `userId` and `orderId`, and must never log email, name, phone, address, passwords, reset tokens or whole user objects. `User` carries a lot of personal data, and `resetPassword` handles a reset token, so those two places need the most care.
